  "summary": "Alameda police used automated license plate readers to locate a stolen vehicle after a carjacking on Brush Street in which the owner was dragged from the car. Investigators identified the suspect, obtained warrants (including for a prior summer armed robbery), and arrested them two days later. The article notes Alameda's expansion of ALPR technology amid broader privacy concerns around vendors like Flock.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Using Automated License Plate Readers, they located the vehicle, though it had already been abandoned and was unoccupied when they found it",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "Automated license plate readers have been around for decades, but the technology has recently drawn more attention amid privacy concerns tied to companies like Flock and allegations that data has been shared with federal immigration authorities",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "A city project described in a request for proposals aimed to add a fixed camera system to the department's existing mobile readers",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    }
  ],
